  "geometryBasis": "Three named public map footprints fix the Old Hall, Chapel and Great Hall/Library. A mapped gate point lies on the Old Buildings street envelope. The Stone Buildings ranges follow the northern estate edges and associated masonry limits.",
  "sectionBasis": "Lincoln’s Inn and the statutory heritage records distinguish the medieval and Victorian red-brick halls, pale open-undercroft chapel, brick gatehouse and eighteenth-century classical Stone Buildings. Exact Qualla and published archive imagery support the entrances and primary materials.",
  "limitations": [
    "Primary named structures and the adjoining Old Buildings are within scope. Other chambers, modern underground facilities, New Square and detached park structures remain part of base Earth context.",
    "Not all small parts have independent surveyed outlines. The Gatehouse’s return, late roof profiles, Stone Buildings court facades and fenestration are rationalized against the mapped blocks and historical sources.",
    "The Great Hall and Library share a mapped outer footprint. Their joining structures, lead and slate roof segmentation, individual stained glass and heraldic panel details are approximated."
  ],
